WEBVTT

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.690
It was not revenge
by the Demonically Possessed.

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:36.740
He was silenced by another human.

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:38.410
You're the one who killed Mr. Mikami!

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:40.450
No way! I would never kill him!

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:44.200
I keep watch over everyone's actions
and comments from here!

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.620
The arsonist is at the scene of the fire.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:49.710
Is that why you killed him, Miles?

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:51.750
Miles Morgan.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:56.840
EPISODE 9
WITHOUT UNDERSTANDING THE TEARS SHED

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:53.710
The closest of all insiders.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.880
A cop from the Anti-Demon Bureau
was the kingpin for the Demonically Possessed.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:01.260
You have anything to say, Chief?

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.220
So?

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:05.600
On what grounds is he the traitor?

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:09.190
I first doubted him...

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:13.860
when I found a strange commonality in the events
right after Demon Hazards occurred.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:15.820
In over half of all incidents...

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:16.610
Affiliation: Anti-Demon Bureau
Male. Married.
Has a wife and
three daughters.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:19.610
and in every case
deemed as a critical hazard...

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:23.120
we found out that the first officer
to arrive on scene was...

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:25.790
Officer Morgan.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.670
If that was all, you could say
he was simply a brilliant officer.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.040
I can't really say that's conclusive.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.420
The arsonist is at the scene of the fire.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:36.010
What?

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.550
We also found
conclusive evidence of course.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.720
Two of the Demonically Possessed...

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:44.810
had contacted individuals with the same tattoo
several days before each incident.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:50.940
Every member of the Anti-Demon Bureau
has identified this individual as Officer Morgan.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:04.370
Oh!

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:07.330
So Akino's out to kill me, too?

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.870
They're giving me
quite the VIP treatment here.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:13.580
Hey Shu, how much is my head worth?

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:18.800
Like I'd know. AAA was the company that won
the auction, so you can ask their president.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:23.340
I see. I hope I got
at least a million dollars, you know.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:29.310
I mean, I may be treated as a B-Class,
but I'm virtually at A-Class level.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:34.560
MIKHAIL HACHISUKA

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.560
<i>What's the meaning of this?</i>

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:37.270
You ask what the meaning of this is, but—

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:39.400
<i>Why did you not stop the auction?</i>

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.900
<i>Why didn't you report this immediately?</i>

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.780
<i>I can't allow for
such a ridiculous auction to happen!</i>

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:48.990
<i>Are you telling me AAA is going to defeat
that Demonically Possessed for just one dollar?</i>

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:54.540
I won't mind if you compensated us
with a fair price, you know.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:55.540
<i>Wha...</i>

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:58.630
That's what you promised
all the other companies, right?

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:01.380
So that you could
get rid of Shu and myself.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:04.970
You're going to exclude
Mr. Ogata from the auction?

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:07.010
AAA isn't looking good, either.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:11.390
I know. Contact the other companies and
have them win the auction at the lowest price.

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.890
I'll compensate them later...

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.150
no matter what the price.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.270
Why would you do that?

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:21.650
Director General, weren't you the one
who leaked information to Mr. Ogata...

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:24.160
to move him as your pawn
for all this time?

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.700
Indeed so.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:30.370
In order to crush every minion of Asmodeus
and seal it away again,

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:33.580
I needed him and his minion's powers.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:39.880
However, if the final target is his foster parent,
it's a completely different matter.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:45.050
I can't let the hero of the City
bear the cross of killing his own parent.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:47.390
Don't you think so?

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.430
<i>You'd heard from Ashiya, right?</i>

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:54.890
<i>This is a tough job for you guys.
Was I mistaken in my decision?</i>

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:59.480
It's true that superficially,
that sounds like an inspiring tale.

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:02.900
But please don't worry.
We're professionals.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:06.700
Whether it be a friend or a foster parent,

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:10.160
we'll defeat that despicable
Demonically Possessed.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.580
<i>What is your real objective?</i>

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.580
<i>What are you hiding from me?</i>

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:19.290
Director General,
what exactly are you hiding?

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:20.590
<i>What?</i>

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.470
You've been relying on Shu
for all this time,

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:28.970
but you distance yourself from him at the very end.
What's the real reason behind that?

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:31.810
<i>How many times do I have to tell you?
I don't want him—</i>

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:33.810
Then, let me answer for you.

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:38.440
You actually know where Shu's family
currently is, don't you?

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:43.070
And you're fearing the fact
that Miles will tell him the exact location.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:47.320
Because you have no intention
of rescuing Shu's family.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:52.830
No, that's not all. If push comes to shove,
you're going to abandon them.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:57.500
<i>Th-That's out of the question! What evidence
do you have to make such a claim—</i>

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:02.340
Evidence? Of course I have nothing of the sort.
That was just a speculation.

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:04.710
<i>Huh?</i>

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:07.340
But with that reaction of yours,
I'm convinced now.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.720
You try to sound threatening
saying you're the head of the police,

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:13.470
but when it comes to negotiations,
you still show your age—

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:15.560
Huh?

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:17.810
He hung up.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:22.610
This is terrible. I wonder
if I'll still receive retirement benefits.

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:27.320
In the worst case,
we'll hire you, so don't worry.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:33.370
Director General!
We have an emergency situation!

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.740
What is it this time?

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.050
Why is it, Miles...

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:55.810
When my dad died,
you looked after me.

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:59.440
You were kind to me
when I had no relatives to turn to.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:04.190
After all that,
why did you side with a demon?

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:09.200
In the end, you fall way short
compared to Mr. Mikami.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:16.790
He only used his feet and his wits
to find his way to the entire truth.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:21.370
I believed that the only ones
who can outsmart me

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:27.050
would be my boss to whom I always report,
or anyone higher up.

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:30.300
But in reality,
there was one more person.

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:34.550
One more person with whom
I always shared my information.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:36.260
That's right.

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:37.430
My partner...

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:39.310
you!

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:41.690
Junya Hanamura.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:44.940
When his name came up
in our investigation...

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:48.610
it took about 15 minutes
for me to report to my boss,

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:52.820
get a search warrant,
and be dispatched together with you.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.450
If you were a Demonically Possessed...

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:58.450
that was more than enough time
to kill him and return.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:00.830
Twelve years ago.

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:05.290
Right when the incident
concerning Mr. Ogata's father happened,

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:08.300
your daughter's illness
turned for the worse.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:11.880
I heard that she even went
into cardiac arrest at one point.

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:15.850
But she had a miraculous recovery since.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:19.100
I prayed to God...

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:22.100
along with some other entity.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:25.440
Your prayers must've been answered.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:29.820
You found a matching donor for her,
and the surgery was a success.

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:33.240
I can't imagine how many miracles you had.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:36.990
So, was it from back then?

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:43.620
You were involved with the case
of Mr. Ogata's father, as well?

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:47.710
Tell me one thing.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:50.250
What exactly is Asmodeus?

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:55.550
My benefactor. I owe so much that I can't
fully repay even if I offer my own life.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:58.550
I see.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:04.560
You're not getting away with this, Miles.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.020
What are you gonna do in that case?

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:09.400
Well, I assume you're gonna kill me.

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:14.900
There's something you need to do
before we talk about killing you or not!

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:16.200
Something I need to do?

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:18.660
Apologize!

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:20.490
Huh?

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:21.870
To Mr. Mikami!

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:24.870
To everyone you duped!

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:27.630
To everyone you killed!
To everyone you deceived!

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:29.960
To the AAA President! To Ayano!

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:31.710
To my family!

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:32.880
And to me!

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.640
You really are a little brat.

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:47.230
Shut up!

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.320
Let me tell you this, Shu.

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:00.410
I have no regrets.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:26.680
Old man!

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:32.400
Fire!

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:42.240
You're gonna leave it up to them?

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:44.950
But... I mean...

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:48.160
your power would kill him!

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:51.000
If he ends up not dying,

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:53.790
and if one of those people
over there were to die...

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:57.550
you would rather have that instead, Shu?

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:02.050
Are you okay feeling the same way
as when you lost Detective Mikami?

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:48.930
Why the hell are you here?

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:52.440
That's quite the attitude
against someone who saved your life.

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:57.730
Shu, did you set her free?

00:11:58.320 --> 00:11:59.360
Yeah.

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:05.240
She demanded two things
as her conditions for teaming up with us.

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:07.030
One was her freedom.

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:13.540
And the other was the memories
of Asmodeus's puppet.

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:15.460
Memories...

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:18.630
Kisara...

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:21.550
I need you to suck out memories
from Miles's brain.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:24.300
I might end up killing him, though.

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:27.050
Then, use all your power to let him die...

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:31.060
in exchange for every memory of Miles left in me.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:34.100
If you lost that many memories...

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:39.150
<i>Once a tear in your memory expands,
your devotion also becomes sparse.</i>

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:41.940
<i>In due time, you'll no longer feel anything.</i>

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:44.320
<i>Your enemy, your family...</i>

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:47.530
<i>the women you've slept with...</i>

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:50.790
I have to go that far
in order to defeat that enemy!

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:12.980
Outta my way!

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:34.620
Looks like we're no longer needed here.

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:37.710
Then, shall we settle our own score?

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:39.130
Later.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:44.050
Once all the demons are eradicated,
we humans can kill each other.

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:07.780
HE KILLED
MR. MIKAMI!

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:55.330
Please take care... of Shu.

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:56.950
Huh?

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:10.260
You came all the way over here
to be killed!

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:14.810
Die, demon!

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:29.530
You must be Officer Morgan.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:34.950
Inspector Yugiri told me
to trust you if anything happens.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:43.580
Demons? What are they?

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:46.380
Apparently, they're behind the phenomenon

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:50.840
where humans turn into monsters
that's been happening often in the City lately.

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:56.350
Hey, come on! Are you religious or something?
Sorry, but I don't deal with talk of that sort.

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:59.600
Well, that's what everyone says at first.

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:03.400
Wha...

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:07.650
I've hunted down guys like that
all over the world.

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:11.030
Listen up, Miles. Demons exist.

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:14.240
If we don't find their kingpin and defeat it...

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:18.490
peace will never come here to Bayron City!

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:43.560
Hive Three Mine?

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:47.730
Are you saying that's the gates to Hell
where demons pour out of?

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:49.190
It was Orgonium!

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:51.070
It was Orgonium all along!

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:54.700
That miraculous ore
is drawing the demons here!

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:58.200
No, they might even be
actual shards of demons!

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:02.500
If that's true, it's all over for this City.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:05.710
Yeah. That's why we need
a more detailed investigation.

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:07.670
I'm asking the mayor right now—

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:11.210
Sorry, but I'm gonna drop out from this case.

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:17.720
I want to be at Melissa's side for now.

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:30.570
She'll be saved?

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:32.360
N-No, wait!

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:34.860
But humans can't do something like that!

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:39.070
Can it be that you...

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:44.790
<i>This is our regular report.
No abnormalities over here.</i>

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:47.880
Roger that. Please keep it up.

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:50.000
Hey, Akino...

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:52.000
Miles...

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:55.840
Is it all right for you
to not be with Melissa?

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:58.930
I can't do anything
even if I was at her side.

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:03.680
I'll take over.
You can go eat or something.

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:04.810
But...

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.560
Please let me take over.

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:09.810
Doing something
is more likely to keep me distracted.

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:25.960
Why?

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.580
Why, Sayuri?

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:32.960
Kanna is the daughter of you and me.

00:18:33.590 --> 00:18:35.710
A child between a human and a demon.

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:38.630
She will connect you and me.

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:42.180
She will be the gate
that connects humans and demons.

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:57.820
Killing Shu wasn't in the contract, was it?

00:18:58.150 --> 00:18:59.240
That said...

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:02.530
there's no real need
to keep him alive, either.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:10.290
Let me do as I please,
at least this little bit, Sayuri. No...

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:12.540
Asmodeus.

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.280
Your life was spared.

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:42.740
You were unconscious for three days.

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:44.660
What about Shu?

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:47.750
Thanks to you risking your life
and jumping in there,

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:50.120
he was the only survivor.

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:55.710
What about Isamu?

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:58.170
Sayuri? Kanna?

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:02.800
They're under the ocean
along with the entire mine.

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:06.720
I never thought all of Isamu's
speculations were correct.

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:08.560
That explosion...

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:11.690
Was it really a demon's doing, though?

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:12.390
Huh?

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:13.900
Who else would be there?

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:21.070
Never mind.

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:22.740
Mr. Morgan!

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:27.370
Your daughter! Your daughter
has regained consciousness!

00:20:35.840 --> 00:20:38.800
From today on,
this is going to be your home, Shu.

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:49.390
Dear...

00:20:58.570 --> 00:21:02.950
This letter was written by you and
sent by you. You'll continue
fulfilling your end of the contract.

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:26.840
I reside within your subconscious.

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:36.480
How was it, Kisara?

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:39.860
Were you able to get any good information
from that guy's memories?

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:44.610
He said, "I'm sorry."

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:47.240
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:50.780
This Morgan guy pretended to be
Mr. Mikami's subordinate for all this time,

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:53.250
but he was a tool for a demon!
He's the worst—

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:01.050
I'm sorry, Shu.

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:04.510
Die, demon!

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:13.520
Huh?

00:22:14.060 --> 00:22:15.390
What?

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:18.730
Why am I...

00:23:55.620 --> 00:24:00.040
EPISODE 10
HIGH HOPES FOR THE WORST CASE

00:23:56.620 --> 00:23:58.950
"High Hopes for the Worst Case."
